# Gate 2: P01 first-pass proof and priority review

The main trichotomy and codebook arguments survive independent line-by-line mathematical review. This clears a research draft, not a priority-certified submission. Modal nonlocality, Hardy arguments, field dense coding/teleportation, the contextuality hierarchy and Smith/module theory are imported background.

## Proposed contribution paragraph (reported before introduction drafting)
For nonzero bipartite matrices over a finite commutative chain ring, we classify complete-basis support contextuality by nonzero Smith rank and leading multiplicity. Under a fixed-orbit exact communication contract, the same leading multiplicity determines the largest codebook. We distinguish these resources from universal exact teleportation and identify the assumptions on preparation, tensor products and measurements needed for each comparison.

## Proof clearance
- Hyperplane criterion: complement of the union of selected rays cannot contain a residue basis. All lifts outside a containing hyperplane must be selected somewhere. This uses complete settings, and applies to finite local rings.
- Smith invariance: independent GL changes relabel the complete local basis families. No positive inner product is used.
- Rank-one locality: retain a supported seed and choose unit first coordinates elsewhere; the seed hypothesis prevents annihilation in mixed pairs.
- Leading multiplicity >=2: choose a residue row not proportional to the opposite hyperplane functional, then cancel the radical dot product using a unit coordinate. A zero residue contraction alone would not suffice.
- Hardy witness: retain minus c outside characteristic two; embed the 2x2 block and explicitly rule out extra outcomes in each forcing step.
- Codebook: leading disjoint supports bound the number by dh; lift residue-independent orbit images to part of a basis and invert it. Division by pi^a means choosing a preimage, not inverting a nonunit.
- Teleportation: a nonzero singular branch collides on x and x+k, both possible. Completeness excludes all-zero transfers. Equality is raw-vector equality, including reference systems.
- Analyzer extension: GL_d(k) spans Mat_d(k), even over F2; choose d^2 independent invertibles and lift to K. The reshapes and the flattened analysis matrix are separately invertible. This is an elementary corollary, not claimed as an original matrix theorem.
- Two-setting proof: choose an inclusion-minimal support set; for local rings use a nonzero radical layer and an F2-linear functional. Coincident reduced bases cause no exception.

